  {
   "id": "L2",
   "subject": "Work: the name you lost",
   "chapter": "Work: the name you lost",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Nine o'clock. A meeting with new people. Everyone goes around the table and says their name and their role.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2016/05/12/3132-166335897_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2022/10/31/137264-766326227_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The person next to you says their name. Then it's your turn. You say yours.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2020/06/12/41820-431406508_large.mp4",
      "https://pixabay.com/get/gd829820519bccf7509a9cfcd32c682589a36497fdaef5adaca7174dce802e396c72b07c63f30484d6cca7631117257fe82774ab4ed7cbebbc196427b40a4e12e_1280.jpg"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "And by the end of the meeting, you have no idea what the person next to you was called. They were right next to you.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2024/06/13/216597_large.mp4",
      "https://pixabay.com/get/g698edd24a56b7dc4d618118e5884ab79a6eb96a2bc4025cf83eeb003741ab6b506cbd1f5ef517d5e53aeef9c3df0585dd29493b74351d481d5ee4af9542d6d22_1280.jpg",
      "https://pixabay.com/get/g321622843547447f52957c2b0003036385bdb36e126cb1c20f164843e505a117ce2d51ca1a6f2d748117fa074a09c0d071d259e657db7380b810dcf34ba7148a_1280.jpg"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "This has a name: the next-in-line effect.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2019/01/09/20564-310898376_medium.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "In one study, students sat around a table and took turns reading words out loud.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2025/02/04/256411_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2024/06/06/215474_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Later they had to remember every word they had heard.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2022/06/27/122233-724743712_medium.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2025/05/06/277042_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "They remembered their own words very well, nearly nine in ten.",
     "clips": [
      "repo:assets/2026-11-21-long/d04_nextinline_a.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "But the words read just before their turn, and just after it, were remembered worst of all.",
     "clips": [
      "repo:assets/2026-11-21-long/d05_nextinline_b.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The closer a word came to their own turn, the more likely it was to vanish.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2018/11/21/19456-303877307_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2020/08/13/47064-450094991_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Here's why. When your turn is coming, your brain is busy getting ready. What will I say? How will I sound?",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2023/11/02/187516-880665394_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2016/05/12/3161-166338902_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "There isn't room left to store what the person next to you is saying.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2021/11/08/95122-645704287_medium.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2021/11/08/95126-645704295_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Then, while you speak and calm down afterward, the same thing happens again.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2024/03/16/204420-924209370_medium.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2023/01/26/148048-793525179_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "And names have a second problem. Researchers have found that it is much harder to remember that a person's name is Baker than to remember that a person is a baker.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2024/03/28/205889_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2021/02/15/65278-514138802_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2020/06/14/42040-431422845_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2024/03/28/205890_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "It's the same word.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2022/11/29/140931-776453915_medium.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2025/02/16/258562_medium.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The reason is meaning. A baker connects to a hundred things you already know: bread, early mornings, flour on their hands.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2021/01/27/63066-505518648_medium.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2024/04/15/207994_medium.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2018/02/10/14239-255658087_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Mr. Baker connects to almost nothing. A name is a label with no story attached.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2021/03/12/67763-523386873_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2016/05/12/3173-166338972_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Your brain is built to keep stories.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2023/04/16/159245-818219773_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2022/12/20/143683-784129669_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "So if you want to keep a name, give it a story. Link it to something. Say it back once, out loud, after your own turn is over.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2022/09/08/130648-747868373_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2023/04/16/159243-818219768_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2023/07/11/171044-844787782_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Again, notice what your brain is doing. It isn't broken.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2021/06/28/79387-569653286_medium.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "It's protecting what matters most to it in that moment: your own turn, and things that connect to what you already know.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2023/08/24/177474-857714980_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2018/10/14/18713-295718392_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2020/07/04/43843-437611786_large.mp4"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "But what about the things you work hard to learn? Surely those stay. Not so fast.",
     "clips": [
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2021/03/31/69625-531621058_large.mp4",
      "https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2022/07/15/124252-730508538_large.mp4"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "settings": {
    "video_aspect": "16:9",
